=EF=BB=BFWhen asked, I always answer "sure, you could run something like Ub=
untu on=20
these boards".

But then when someone asks the obvious next question: "Oh, nice, how do I d=
o=20
that?" I usually suddenly remember that I had some very urgent business els=
ewhere.

So I'd like to forward this one to the list. There's plenty boards out ther=
e=20
now with big CPUs and supporting big screens and all. If I wanted to turn s=
uch=20
not-so-mainstream board into a real desktop, how does one do that?

It's really easy to find desktop distro's for Intel/AMD PCs. But once your=
=20
machine runs on ARM or MIPS, all you can find is some vague references, and=
 if=20
you're really lucky, some binary blob that happens to run on a particular b=
oard.

The OE layers I could find, all seem to restrict themselves to small device=
s=20
with even smaller screens, and won't give you much more than a clunky music=
=20
player.


